# `merge=union` keeps the lines from BOTH sides of a conflicting hunk instead of
# writing conflict markers. It is built into git, so it needs no per-developer
# `git config` — cloning the repo is enough for it to take effect.
#
# docs/DRIFT-TO-VELOCITY.md is append-mostly: nearly every branch adds one row to
# the §6 change-log table, and two branches adding different rows at the same
# position conflict every single time even though the resolution is always "keep
# both". Union merge does that automatically.
#
# The tradeoff, because it is not free: union applies to the WHOLE file, not just
# the table, and gitattributes cannot scope to a region. So when two branches edit
# the SAME existing line differently — rewording a §2/§4/§5 paragraph, say — you
# get both versions kept silently rather than a conflict to resolve. Review the
# merged section when a change edits existing prose rather than appending a row.
#
# Applies to merge, rebase and cherry-pick (all use the merge machinery).
docs/DRIFT-TO-VELOCITY.md merge=union
